<title>SWEDEN: Volvo's new CEO says alliances, takeovers natural.</title>
<headline>Volvo's new CEO says alliances, takeovers natural.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new chief executive of AB Volvo, Leif Johansson, said on Monday that it was natural for the Swedish vehicle manufacturer to look at alliances or takeovers.</p>
<p>Johansson, who will take over from Soren Gyll at the end of April, also said it was essential for Volvo to develop a strong, niche strategy for its car unit.  </p>
<p>&quot;In this type of sector, either concerning cars or white goods, it is natural to look at alliances,&quot; Johansson told a news conference.</p>
<p>Asked if there could be an alliance in cars, Johansson said: &quot;I think that you can't rule out anything but right now we want to chisel out a strong, niche strategy for cars.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
